    "ssky_text_block_8H6XVj": {
      "type": "ssky-text-block",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_kYqRnd": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<p>You Want to Raise Free-Thinking, Freedom-Loving Individuals </p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "heading_weight": "bold",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "center": false
          }
        },
        "text_nxbMcM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 72,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>But it’s hard to navigate the minefield of media and entertainment manipulation, right?</p>",
            "text_size": "extra-large",
            "text_weight": "medium"
          }
        },
        "text_88kqHC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 120,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>You have probably tried in the past to educate your kids on what’s happening in our world and struggled:<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "medium"
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_4KejYf": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text": "<p>A trip to the <strong>Local Library </strong>in search of good literature results in frustration that many books are pushing harmful agendas that are appealing to kids. You wonder what good material you can introduce to your children that they’ll actually enjoy.</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "icon_b": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text_b": "<p>You have broached big subjects in <strong>Family Discussions </strong>after dinner that end up in silence from apathetic kids or end awkwardly when your kids ask questions you can’t answer.</p>",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_cH8aQj": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text": "<p>After finding <strong>YouTube Videos</strong> from creators that seemed good at the time for your kids, you discovered that they ultimately had some agenda and were using their platform to promote ideas you strongly disagree with.</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "icon_b": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text_b": "<p>Perhaps you use <strong>Current Events</strong> to try and educate your child about what is happening but there is no context and it’s too complex to explain. Often, you wonder if what you’re doing is enough to “stick” and prepare your children for the world they’re growing up in.</p>",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "divider_pF39QX": {
          "type": "divider",
          "settings": {
            "margin": 24,
            "contrast": true
          }
        },
        "text_cGkQPz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 92,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>Your kids are sometimes left with more questions than answers, and you can’t bear the thought of them getting lost at sea in all the manipulation and power games playing out in the world. <br/><br/>What if the solution to this emerging education problem was simpler than you thought?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "semibold"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
